# Oplyra database migrations (Flask-Migrate / Alembic)

## Development / testing

By default the app still runs `db.create_all()` for convenience.

## Production

`ProductionConfig.USE_ALEMBIC_ONLY = True` skips `create_all`. Apply schema with:

```bash
export FLASK_ENV=production
export SECRET_KEY="$(python -c "import secrets; print(secrets.token_hex(32))")"
export DATABASE_URL="mysql+pymysql://..."
flask db upgrade
```

## Generating a new revision

```bash
# Compare models to an empty DB (avoid create_all during generate):
set OPLYRA_SKIP_DB_INIT=1
flask db migrate -m "describe change"
flask db upgrade
```

## Existing databases that already have tables

```bash
flask db stamp head
```
